# rule.forbid.undefined-inputs

never use undefined for an internal contract input; use null (or [] for a list). scope: the `input` arg of (input, context) on every contract outside src/contract/; context and options args exempt
why: a null must be supplied on purpose, so the compiler surfaces each forgotten input up the call stack; an optional attribute hides it
exception: user-faced contracts in src/contract/ may use optional attributes for ux
```ts
// 👍 nullable, supplied on purpose
input: { exid: string; assignedTo: Ref<typeof Delegate> | null; excludeIds: string[] }
// 👎 optional in an internal contract
input: { exid: string; assignedTo?: Ref<typeof Delegate> }
```
enforcement: optional attribute or undefined value in an internal input = blocker
see also: rule.require.input-context-pattern · rule.forbid.undefined-attributes
